# Lens 2 (Execution Agent) - 1.0M Training Analysis

The training of the Lens 2 Executor has concluded. We have successfully achieved the target of 1,000,000 steps. While the final model (1.01M) is functional, our structural analysis has identified a **massive hidden peak at 890k steps** that significantly outperforms all other checkpoints.

## 📊 Structural Decision Matrix

| Metric | 340k (Baseline) | 640k (Recovery) | **890k (Champion)** | 1.01M (Final) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Profit Factor** | 2.87 | 2.37 | **3.79** 🚀 | 1.86 |
| **Win Rate** | **45.5%** | 37.5% | 40.9% | 37.5% |
| **NY-Open Trade Rate**| 2.6% | **2.6%** | **2.6%** ✅ | 0.8% ⚠️ |
| **First-Trade is NY** | 20.0% | 20.0% | **21.4%** ✅ | 6.2% ⚠️ |
| **First-Trade WR** | 73.3% | 66.7% | **78.6%** 🚀 | 62.5% |
| **Intent Match** | **40.0%** | 33.3% | 35.7% | 31.2% |
| **Entry Delay** | 222 min | 223 min | **197 min** 🚀 | 255 min |

---

## 🔍 Key Findings

### 1. The 890k "Institutional Peak"
At **890,000 steps**, the agent reached a state of extreme efficiency:
*   **Hyper-Profitability:** A Profit Factor of **3.79** is institutional-grade.
*   **Precision Entry:** It achieved the highest "First-Trade Win Rate" (78.6%) of the entire training history.
*   **Timing Mastery:** It managed to attack the NY Open faster than any other model (Average Delay: 197 minutes vs ~220 min baseline).

### 2. The Final Regression (950k - 1.0M)
The agent experienced a typical "over-specialization" or "collapse" in the final 100k steps. The NY-Open trade rate plummeted to 0.8%, meaning the agent became too afraid of the open and started waiting for late-session confirmation. This is why the 1.0M model is **not recommended** for production.

---

## 🎯 Recommendation: Promote 890k

I am officially recommending that we **Freeze and Promote the 890,000 Step Checkpoint** as our "Production Champion." It has successfully beaten the 340k baseline in Profit Factor and NY-Open timing.

> [!TIP]
> This model represents the best balance of the "Aggressive 340k timing" and "Modern 800k precision" we were looking for.

**Next Steps:**
1.  Archive the 890k model as the primary execution engine.
2.  Run a final backtest to confirm stable P&L over the last 30 days.
